SM(633,{"n":"Revelation 21-22","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Revelation 21-22.mp3","d":2483.0,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.24,"Chapter 21. Now I saw a new heaven and a new earth."],[24.72,"For the first heaven and the first earth had passed away."],[28.4,"Also there was no more sea."],[30.72,"Sorry, beachgoers. No, that's not what it's talking about."],[34.88,"So when did the old heaven and the old earth pass away?"],[39.76,"Remember, they ran away."],[42.56,"They ran away from God on the throne."],[46.56,"They sort of scampered off."],[48.18,"So that is a new one."],[49.3,"So, what is it talking about?"],[50.34,"Is it talking about like the physical earth?"],[53.62,"Well, then it would have to be talking about the physical heaven."],[58.42,"So, no. Um, it's talking about the order of the creation."],[67.72,"That's why it's using heaven and earth."],[69.72,"So, where does Genesis?"],[71.4,"We'll get there in a couple weeks."],[72.76,"Where does Genesis 1 start?"],[74.36,"In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth."],[79.0,"And so now we've got a new heavens and a new earth."],[82.32,"And as we'll talk about more in Genesis 1, what it's really about is not making something appear out of thin air in Genesis 1."],[90.8,"I'm not denying that God created out of nothing."],[93.28,"I'm saying that's not what Genesis 1 is about."],[95.44,"Genesis 1 is about God putting things in order."],[98.66,"So there's a new order."],[100.5,"Why is there a new order in heaven?"],[103.58,"Because there's no more demonic spirits."],[106.4,"Demons out, humans in."],[109.17,"And why is there a new order on earth?"],[112.63,"Because now justice has been established."],[114.79,"That's what judgment is."],[116.15,"Judgment is establishing justice, putting things back in order."],[120.23,"So it's new."],[121.76,"That old order has passed away that had been corrupted by sin."],[127.44,"Now there's this new order that's like that original order, which remember God looked at everything and saw that it was good."],[133.92,"And the word good there, T tomovee, also means beautiful."],[137.09,"Whole. We're back to that, is the idea here."],[140.85,"And why is there no sea?"],[143.65,"C is a symbol of chaos."],[145.37,"There is no more destruction"],[145.39,"C is about chaos and destruction."],[148.59,"There is no more chaos."],[152.03,"This isn't going to repeat itself."],[154.27,"The last cycle is over."],[156.05,"No more cycles."],[160.37,"Verse 2, then I, John, saw the holy city, New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband."],[172.77,"We already saw the wedding supper of the Lamb language used."],[178.1,"So we have the new Jerusalem."],[180.27,"The new city of God."],[182.37,"And what's a city?"],[184.21,"It's again an order, it's a community."],[186.99,"It's an ordered community of humans."],[189.05,"So we've now come humans are going to be in this new sort of community communal order that comes down from heaven."],[196.33,"And I heard a loud voice from heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people."],[204.41,"God himself will be with them and be their God."],[224.81,"That old order that was full of suffering and sin, hardship, death, all that's over now."],[233.26,"And God is now dwelling with his people."],[236.62,"Why is that so important?"],[238.22,"Well, how did all of that death and mourning and crying start?"],[243.34,"Humanity was expelled from paradise."],[246.98,"So now that's restored."],[248.42,"Now humanity is in the presence of God again."],[254.9,"Verse 5. Then he who sat on the throne said, Behold, I make all things new."],[260.34,"And he said to me, Write, for these words are true and faithful."],[265.3,"And he said to me, It is done."],[267.06,"I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end."],[270.58,"I will give of the fountain of the water of life freely to him who thirsts."],[276.46,"We'll pause there."],[277.84,"So we're back to where we started."],[279.78,"Remember? When Christ told him he was the Alpha and the Omega."],[283.32,"So you can tell we're wrapping up here."],[286.18,"That um so he returns to that language, the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning of the end."],[292.34,"Notice that I'll give of the fountain of the water of life freely to him who thirsts."],[297.38,"That's actually something Christ said in St."],[299.78,"John's Gospel. Remember on the last day of the feast, the last great day of the feast, stood up and said, Let he who is thirsty come to me and drink."],[310.34,"John's Gospel talked to St"],[310.83,"He also in St."],[313.55,"Fochini, the Samaritan woman, about the living water."],[316.92,"Water of life."],[320.1,"So this is one of many places where we could see that this is the same Saint John for anybody who's doubting."],[330.82,"Verse 7, he who overcomes shall inherit all things, and I will be his God, and he shall be my son."],[341.54,"So why is it son?"],[343.3,"Is it just because we're all misogynists and don't use inclusive language in the distant past?"],[348.98,"No, it's because we're talking about inheritance."],[352.34,"And the culture in which this was written."],[355.03,"Sons inherited. And that was pretty much it."],[359.13,"So he's not just talk talking toing to men. men, he's and women, that they become sons"],[365.33,"So if he had in the first century said, You will become sons and daughters, that would have applied to the original readers that there was still gonna be this status distinction in the life of the world to come."],[377.73,"So St. John is very deliberately saying, as St."],[380.53,"Paul did when he talked about inheritance and becoming sons of God, he's very deliberately saying that that status difference is not something that's in this order."],[392.57,"That everyone becomes an an inheritor."],[398.25,"And uh notice that he who overcomes, the one who overcomes."],[404.11,"Which we saw over again in the letters."],[419.87,"Shall have their part in the lake which burns with fire in brimstone, which is the second death."],[427.39,"So notice what the contrast is."],[430.43,"Contrast is between the one who overcomes, the one who is victorious, and then these types of folks."],[437.55,"So, what does that imply about these types of folks?"],[440.91,"There was some kind of struggle, and they lost."],[447.47,"So this is how sin."],[455.43,"Sin, the passions."],[457.49,"So the liar is not the person who told a lie once when they were five."],[464.93,"The liar is the one who gives in the passionate who becomes a liar."],[470.54,"Who becomes cowardly."],[473.74,"It's not the person who watches or does something sexually immoral. because they let lust take over their life"],[483.82,"Rather than struggling."],[492.66,"Verse 9. Then one of the seven angels who had the seven bowls, filled with the seven last plagues, came to me and talked with me, saying, Come, I will show you the bride of the lamb, the bride, the lamb's wife."],[505.48,"So we had the wedding supper of the Lamb."],[512.76,"And he carried me away in the spirit to a great and high mountain, and showed me the great city, the holy Jerusalem, descending out of heaven from God, having the glory of God."],[524.84,"Her light was like a most precious stone, like a jasper stone clear as crystal."],[530.52,"Verse 12 So he's going to see the city, which comes down from heaven."],[536.4,"Also she had a great and high wall with twelve gates, and twelve angels at the gates, and names written on them, which are the names of the twelve tribes of the children of Israel."],[547.84,"Actually, it's the sons of Israel, because you know the tribes were named after the twelve sons."],[554.08,"Um we have the gates are named after the twelve tribes."],[558.48,"Three gates on the east, three gates on the north, three gates on the south, and three gates on the west."],[570.57,"The gateways into the kingdom are the twelve tribes of Israel."],[576.89,"Remember things we talked about in the past with St."],[579.13,"Paul, like in Romans 10 and 11."],[580.33,"Verse 14 Now the wall of the city had 12 foundations, and on them were the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb."],[594.53,"So note the parallel."],[597.33,"Twelve and twelve."],[599.17,"But also, um, this is very similar to imagery that we saw St."],[604.69,"Paul use. About the apostles laying a foundation."],[609.67,"Christ is the chief cornerstone."],[612.55,"And then the members of the church building on that, in their lives."],[617.01,"So this city, following that analogy, has been built."],[622.43,"Has been built by God's people."],[622.91,"By the church"],[634.45,"And he who talked with me had a gold reed to measure the city, its gates, and its wall."],[641.01,"So uh this is picking up from Ezekiel's vision of the temple, which is like the last third or so of the book of Ezekiel."],[651.25,"Uh we'll eventually wrap around and get to it."],[654.21,"Uh couple of years."],[656.13,"Um, but um, probably three, four years."],[659.81,"Um but uh Ezekiel's temple is interpreted as being uh prophetic of Christ, who is going to be the eternal temple."],[670.89,"But we're picking up on this with the city."],[674.25,"So the idea here is that St."],[678.65,"John wants us to be thinking in terms of imagery and numbers and symbolism."],[685.77,"We're going to see that this is not the literal measurements of a city."],[700.09,"And he measured the city with the reed, 12,000 furlongs."],[703.61,"Its length, breadth, and height are equal."],[709.69,"I like how they handily translated Greek measurements into furlongs that we're all used to."],[718.69,"We're all used to using uh as a measurement."],[722.45,"Um did they at least in the footnotes give us a uh this Bible says stadia, which makes no more sense."],[729.25,"Yeah, exactly. Well that's the original."],[730.94,"Stadia is the original."],[732.62,"Yeah. It's just 12 times 1,000 C equals 1,500 miles per city."],[737.98,"Okay. Okay. So 1,500 miles uh is what we do with those furlongs."],[743.58,"Um, but you'll also notice that's its heights, height, breadth, and width."],[750.46,"Meaning it's a giant cube."],[752.06,"So this is not the Borg landing on Earth for Star Trek fans."],[756.14,"But yeah, so we we're're not talking literal here."],[758.98,"He's not saying there's gonna be a 1500 mile cube city that we're all gonna live in in the new heavens of the new earth."],[770.74,"Note that with a stadia, it's 12 times a thousand."],[775.02,"A thousand is big number."],[777.9,"Twelve is the number of gates we've had, the number of foundations we have."],[781.28,"That's that's what's being worked with here."],[785.68,"Okay. Verse 17."],[787.76,"Then he measured its wall, 144 cubits, according to the measure of a man, that is of an angel."],[797.25,"So that again, so a cu.bit is the distance from your elbow to your fingertip"],[805.93,"How big is an angel's arm?"],[808.57,"Beats me. So again, we're not to take this literally."],[814.23,"That's why he says, according to a man, and then he says, that is an angel."],[817.77,"To say, hey, what angel cubits, you don't know how long that is."],[822.71,"Like, but what's 144?"],[825.11,"It's 12 times 12."],[828.04,"So I mean, 12 right is two sixties."],[831.17,"So it's like supposed to be like doubly finished or something."],[834.93,"Is that countless what I mean?"],[836.53,"No, I think it's again riffing off of the 12 tribes of the 12 apostles."],[841.25,"That it's 12 by twelve."],[849.02,"Eighteen. Verse eighteen."],[850.78,"The construction of its wall was of jasper, and the city was pure gold like clear glass."],[858.06,"So a giant gold clear cube."],[865.02,"The foundation you could picture it."],[867.92,"You could just picture this exactly whatever."],[870.16,"Um the foundations of the wall of the city were adorned with all kinds of precious stones."],[875.68,"The first foundation was Jasper, the second Sapphire, the third Chalcedoni, the fourth emerald, the fifth Sardonyx, the sixth Sardius, the seventh chrysalite, the eighth barrel, the ninth.inth Topaz, the tenth Chrysopras, the eleventh Jash, and the twelfth Ametyst"],[891.4,"You can figure out which one's which apostle."],[894.44,"I'm not worrying about it."],[896.36,"Is this related to the one the other?"],[899.16,"These are the foundations, which were the number of the apostles, he said."],[902.2,"But the stones, aren't those related to the priestly?"],[906.36,"Yes. Yeah, yeah, yeah."],[908.12,"They're not the same ones."],[911.0,"There were, yeah, in the what he's referring to is in the high priest's Ephid in the Torah, he had stones with the names, precious stones in the Ephod with the names of the twelve tribes on them."],[925.85,"But these don't exactly match in terms and try to figure out which apostle is which."],[930.01,"Like I said, have fun"],[934.21,"Another notable thing is I couldn't go to my local jewelry and say I want to ring with Telson on me now."],[939.81,"Yeah. Yeah. So everywhere we're seeing this again, this parallel."],[948.93,"Remember, we had the 24 elders, and we said part of that was that it's a third of the elders."],[955.19,"And the other part was that it's two twelves."],[957.12,"Like the twelve patriarchs of the twelve apostles."],[960.82,"So we're still getting sort of rifts on that here."],[963.84,"This connection between well, the twelve apostles who are gonna sit on twelve thrones and judge the twelve tribes of Israel."],[970.66,"This this connection."],[975.18,"Verse 21, the twelve gates were twelve pearls."],[979.18,"Each individual gate was of one pearl."],[982.86,"And the street of the city was pure gold, like transparent glass."],[988.46,"So gold streets in the cube city, and each gate into the city is one single giant pearl."],[1002.28,"Yeah. One big pearl."],[1005.96,"Yeah, there's twelve of them."],[1008.28,"One for each tribe."],[1011.08,"Um, yeah, so again, not literal, but the streets of gold."],[1017.24,"Okay I have to do this"],[1017.52,"I think we have time."],[1021.76,"This will be the light entertainment portion of our Bible study."],[1026.0,"Uh, the greatest sermon I ever heard on TBN, the Trinity Broadcasting Network, from Paul Crouch, CEO of the Trinity Broadcasting Network."],[1041.04,"During a like telethon fun drive, he said, These are the end times."],[1049.2,"End times are upon us."],[1051.04,"Book of Revelation."],[1052.24,"It's coming true every day."],[1055.12,"Because he, of course, had that view that this is a bunch of stuff that's gonna happen in the future."],[1059.04,"He said, The four horsemen of the apocalypse."],[1061.84,"Getting ready to ride out."],[1062.96,"You're up there in heaven getting ready to ride out"],[1064.2,"Getting ready to ride out across the earth."],[1069.48,"They're chomping at the bit."],[1071.24,"They're pawing at the ground."],[1073.4,"You're pawing at them streets of gold."],[1076.12,"You're kicking up dust."],[1078.28,"Gold dust from them streets of gold."],[1081.16,"It's coming down from heaven and landing in the checking accounts of those who write a check right now to Trinity Broadcasting Network."],[1091.24,"And I was just, I was amazed."],[1093.56,"I was like, that I mean, there is some level of artistry and brilliance involved there."],[1098.44,"I'm not sure he's using his powers for good and not for evil."],[1102.2,"But. As I said, the light entertainment portion."],[1105.8,"I just thought that was the most amazing thing I ever. heard"],[1111.36,"I've thought about trying that a few times during fun drives at the church, but I don't think I could sell it as well as he did."],[1120.0,"So verse 22."],[1121.92,"But I saw no temple in it, for the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple."],[1132.24,"Now this is interesting because, of course, as soon as that measuring rod comes out, people reading this are thinking, oh, this is like what Ezekiel saw, the temple, and measured it."],[1140.81,"And we just had this whole measuring thing."],[1143.13,"So the fact that there's not a temple, this is the new Jerusalem."],[1147.66,"That's where the temple was."],[1149.98,"There's no temple because. Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple"],[1154.5,"So what was the temple?"],[1156.66,"Temple is the place where God dwelt."],[1162.15,"So where, according to Saint John, does God eternally dwell among his people?"],[1170.39,"In the Lamb."],[1172.95,"In Christ. If you remember St."],[1177.27,"John's gospel, he's the one who gives us the editorial comment."],[1181.11,"The other gospels record Christ saying, destroy this temple and I'll rebuild it in three days."],[1185.43,"But St. John adds, he was speaking of the temple that is his body, just in case you didn't get it."],[1191.04,"Like parenthetical note."],[1192.66,"Hello. So if you need again, sort of direct confirmation of the tradition in the church fathers of reading Ezekiel's temple in in this sort of symbolic way of talking about the incarnation of Christ, here it is."],[1215.72,"Verse 23, the city has no need of the sun or of the moon to shine in it, for the glory of the Lord illuminated it."],[1223.64,"The Lamb is its light."],[1229.0,"So you don't need why why?"],[1233.32,"Why that? Um the sun and the moon are associated, like in Deuteronomy 4, and the stars of heaven with the angelic powers."],[1245.65,"Specifically there with the angelic powers that got worshipped by the nations."],[1250.51,"Ancient worlds full of sun and moon gods."],[1254.13,"So the idea here isn't that like the the uh miasma of incandescent plasma."],[1264.09,"That's 93 million miles from us is going to cease to exist."],[1268.35,"In the new heavens and the new earth, or that the moon is going to cease to exist."],[1271.65,"The idea here is those secondary intermediary powers, those angelic powers, whether they were good or bad, that were between God and humanity, are not in the way anymore."],[1290.41,"It's direct. Direct to God, direct to the Lamb."],[1299.95,"Verse 24. And so it's not coincidental."],[1302.97,"We're talking about the sun and the moon aren't there."],[1304.89,"And the nations of those who are saved shall walk in its light, and the kings of the earth bring their glory and honor into it."],[1312.17,"These are the Gentiles."],[1314.25,"Nations, the Gentiles."],[1316.42,"They're going to walk in the light of what?"],[1318.42,"God Himself, not the Sun and the Moon."],[1324.94,"Verse 25, its gates shall not be shut at all by day, and there's no night."],[1330.7,"There shall be no night there."],[1332.86,"Which is a crazy way to say it."],[1334.94,"But it's split up."],[1339.02,"Yeah, yeah. But so, yeah, the gates open all day, and by the way, it's always day."],[1344.8,"Um, what's the idea there?"],[1346.48,"Well, you don't have to close the gates because there's no threats."],[1349.76,"There's no dangers out there."],[1351.86,"There's nothing. They had to actually close the gates during the day while the work was happening."],[1359.3,"So because they were under assault, under threat."],[1362.68,"And so now there's no threat, there's no gates can just be wide open all the time."],[1370.32,"And they shall bring the glory and the honor of the nations into it."],[1375.18,"This is not only, again, talking about the Gentiles, all the nations coming in."],[1379.77,"This is again connecting to things in Isaiah."],[1383.02,"And uh, well, especially Isaiah, that talk about the nations coming to Jerusalem, to worship the God of Israel."],[1393.3,"St. John sees this happening in Christianity and culminating, at the end."],[1403.23,"Verse 27, but there shall by no means enter anything that defiles or causes. an abomination or a lie, but only those who are written in the Lamb's book of life"],[1413.11,"This is again hammering home that this isn't, just come as you are."],[1421.97,"Or as you were."],[1423.54,"Um try not to do the nirvana reference, but I kind of already did."],[1428.98,"Um this isn't just, you know, all the pagans are now fine."],[1434.48,"Point is they're not pagans anymore."],[1438.7,"They've come to worship the true God, the God of Israel."],[1442.79,"And so they're not bringing with them, when it says they're bringing in the glory of the nations, they're not bringing the idolatry."],[1448.55,"They're not bringing the right, they're not bringing the dedication to conquest and war."],[1454.61,"They're not bringing any of that."],[1456.71,"They're bringing themselves and they're bringing what what is good and pure and holy and beautiful from all the nations."],[1465.53,"Together. Chapter 22, verse 1."],[1474.17,"And he showed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding from the throne of God and of the Lamb."],[1484.73,"Notice it's proceeding from the throne."],[1488.09,"Why is that important?"],[1490.33,"Well, because in the depiction of the judgment in Daniel 7, that was just referred to, there was a river of fire that proceeded from the throne."],[1502.23,"And judgment. So judgment is done."],[1509.67,"So now we have this pure, clear water that gives life."],[1515.44,"That proceeds from the throne."],[1518.4,"So that judgment part is over."],[1520.4,"That enmity part is over."],[1526.64,"Verse 2, in the middle of the street, on either side of the river was the tree of life."],[1534.0,"Now try and figure, try and map that out in your head."],[1536.8,"In the middle of the street and on either side of the river was the tree singular of life, which bore twelve fruits, each tree each yielding its fruit every month."],[1552.52,"I don't think that tree should be added there."],[1555.32,"The idea is that there's twelve."],[1556.92,"There's one for each month."],[1559.32,"Twelve fruits. The leaves of the tree for the healing of the nations."],[1574.24,"So um the uh the tree of life, of course, is the tree of life from paradise."],[1586.21,"So we're having this new city connected directly to the original paradise, because this is a place where the presence of God is."],[1594.95,"That had four rivers throughout of it."],[1596.71,"Here we have this one river of life."],[1598.79,"Um and the uh the tree of life, remember, is what human beings had to be kept away from."],[1607.43,"Because if they ate of the tree of life, they would live forever in the state they were currently in."],[1617.0,"So the fact that now the tree of life is available and everyone is eating from it continually, that's the idea of twelve fruits, one for each month."],[1626.52,"This is continual."],[1627.08,"Meaning that the state of blessedness that they're now in is permanent"],[1633.31,"Is eternal. So there's no chance of oops, somebody messed up again."],[1640.27,"Gotta repeat the whole dern thing."],[1644.96,"Um, that this state is now uh permanent."],[1649.65,"And even just the leaves from it, let alone the fruit, but the leaves, heal those who are coming in, heal them how."],[1659.93,"Well, it's talking about the uncleanness, all of the things that they were exposed to out in the nations."],[1666.66,"And their purification."],[1670.3,"Verse 3, and there shall be no more curse, but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it, and his servants shall serve him."],[1679.42,"Why is no more curse?"],[1681.34,"Remember? The curse is getting sent out of paradise."],[1686.72,"So you're never going to get sent out again."],[1689.14,"Reiterate again. This is this is permanent."],[1692.18,"This is forever."],[1695.14,"They shall see his face, and his name shall be on their foreheads."],[1701.06,"There shall be no night there."],[1703.14,"They need no lamp nor light of the sun, for the Lord God gives them light, and they shall reign forever and ever."],[1714.78,"So he sees this, this is the state, of blessedness in the end."],[1722.88,"Verse 6. Then he said to me, These words are faithful and true."],[1727.12,"And the Lord God of the Holy Prophets sent his angel to show his servants the things which must shortly take place."],[1749.04,"Shortly. 9596 AD"],[1750.6,"In ninety six AD."],[1755.6,"Shortly thereafter. Not once Jack Fenimpee has a TV show."],[1765.32,"Jack passed away, but he's Belgian, so I keep picking on him."],[1773.64,"Verse 7. Behold, I am coming quickly."],[1777.16,"Blessed is he who keeps the words of the prophecy of this book."],[1783.08,"So who's that talking?"],[1786.36,"That's Christ. Who's coming?"],[1791.46,"Notice, coming quickly."],[1794.82,"Not, you know, a long time in the future after all this stuff happens in sequence."],[1801.66,"So Christ's return, Christ's appearing is always imminent."],[1807.82,"You'll sometimes hear scholars say, well, look, in the New Testament, the apostles all thought Jesus was going to come in their lifetime."],[1815.74,"They were wrong."],[1817.66,"It's like, no."],[1819.9,"They thought that, and so did the second generation of Christians, and the third generation of Christians, and the fourth generation."],[1826.8,"And every generation of Christians now their present day."],[1829.54,"Because it can happen at any time."],[1832.12,"But that alone proves that they didn't think this was a whole series of things that were going to happen in the future."],[1837.42,"There wasn't, there weren't a whole bunch of things that had to happen before Christ could return."],[1841.82,"He could return at any time."],[1842.46,"at any time. And even barring his appearing, we can end up standing before him"],[1850.42,"Because we don't know the length of our lives."],[1858.74,"Now I, John, saw and heard these things."],[1861.7,"And when I heard and saw, I fell down to worship before the feet of the angel who showed me these things."],[1869.46,"And he said to me, how many words they added."],[1874.58,"See that you do not do that."],[1877.67,"Basically, knock it off."],[1880.39,"For I am your fellow servant, and of your brethren the prophets, and of those who keep the words of this book, worship God."],[1890.6,"So now, the word angel appeared to describe this person."],[1895.0,"But angel could also just mean messenger."],[1897.64,"And notice he doesn't identify himself as an angel there."],[1903.48,"He says, I am your fellow servant and of your brethren the prophets."],[1907.88,"This may again be St."],[1909.32,"John talking to himself."],[1913.08,"And he said to me, Do not seal the words of the prophecy of this book, for the time is at hand."],[1920.36,"Okay. The time is at hand."],[1923.24,"But this is also a reference to Daniel."],[1927.88,"Daniel was told when he received some of the prophecies that St."],[1931.64,"He was told to shut up the book"],[1932.32,"John has been using."],[1936.56,"Because the prophecies were for the future."],[1941.1,"So Christ comes and those things start happening 500 plus years after Daniel lived."],[1950.76,"So this is a contrast here."],[1952.68,"It's like don't shut it up because this stuff's about to happen."],[1957.26,"This is for right now."],[1958.94,"People need to read this right now."],[1964.06,"He who is unjust, let him be unjust still."],[1967.02,"He who is filthy, let him be filthy still."],[1969.82,"He who is righteous, let him be righteous still."],[1972.7,"He who is holy, let him be holy still."],[1976.98,"That's a weird translation."],[1980.1,"That's the translation Johnny Cash read on his last album, so that says something for it."],[1986.42,"But the idea here, the uh the still, he's not saying like, hey man, if you're filthy, just stay filthy."],[1996.6,"But the idea is again the idea of this being in hand."],[2001.82,"This being in hand."],[2003.66,"So if if you're going to make a change, you need to do it now."],[2010.88,"Because this is coming now."],[2014.0,"You don't have time to, hey, you know what?"],[2016.92,"I'm going to be filthy and engage in all kinds of uncleanness, and then, you know, before the end, I'll repent."],[2025.1,"Real quick and be okay."],[2026.87,"It doesn't work that way."],[2032.71,"Verse 12, and behold, I am coming quickly, and my reward is with me, to give to everyone according to his work."],[2040.15,"Once again, according to his work."],[2044.15,"I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end, the first and the last."],[2049.43,"Blessed are those who do his commandments, that they may have the right to the tree of life, and may enter through the gates into the city."],[2057.11,"Once again, keep his commandments."],[2059.83,"And again, as we said, one of those commandments is to repent."],[2065.71,"So sinning does not mean you haven't kept the commandments unless you don't repent."],[2078.75,"Verse 15, but outside are dogs and sorcerers."],[2086.03,"See my heathen dogs."],[2087.55,"They're right here in the Bible."],[2090.19,"But outside are dogs and sorcerers, and sexually immoral and murderers and idolaters, and whoever loves and practices a lie."],[2099.07,"Notice again, it's not anyone who ever told a lie, it's he who loves and practices a lie."],[2105.0,"And idolaters. And notice the language here."],[2110.12,"So this is why there's this diversity of language about eternal condemnation."],[2115.18,"So the lake of fire obviously is one image."],[2117.51,"Outer darkness and madness is one image."],[2119.35,"Here is just being outside."],[2121.85,"These people are in the city enjoying this bliss, and these other people are outside."],[2126.19,"Why are they outside?"],[2128.19,"Remember, the doors are open."],[2132.59,"Twenty-four hours a day."],[2134.53,"The doors are open."],[2135.57,"They're outside because they want to be outside."],[2139.03,"There's nothing keeping them outside."],[2143.83,"I, Jesus, if you want to put here, fine point on it."],[2146.23,"I, Jesus, have sent my angel to testify to you these things in the churches"],[2153.07,"I am the root and the offspring of David, the bright and morning star."],[2159.15,"So that's pretty direct."],[2162.0,"Notice the root and offspring of David."],[2165.22,"So the offspring of David is pretty clear."],[2167.28,"The Messiah, the son of David."],[2169.22,"But notice he's also the root of David."],[2175.88,"Remember what Christ says about uh Psalm 110 or 109 in the in the Greek, which is the most quoted, as I've mentioned before, I know, the most quoted passage of the Old Testament in the New Testament, Psalm 110. specifically in the beginning"],[2191.44,"When everyone was coming to Christ in the last week of his earthly life before the crucifixion, asking him all these questions, and he decided to throw a question back at them, which never went well for them."],[2204.64,"He said, David says, the Lord said to my Lord, sit at my right hand."],[2209.32,"If the Messiah is David's son, why does he call him Lord?"],[2216.14,"If he's descended from David."],[2221.66,"So, yes, Christ as the Messiah is the Davidic king."],[2226.68,"The bud from Jesse's stem."],[2228.92,"He is the Davidic Messiah."],[2232.28,"But it's Christ's kingship"],[2236.24,"Christ's Messiahship that was really the basis for David's."],[2241.84,"The root and the basis for David's, the paradigm for David's."],[2245.28,"Because Christ is eternal."],[2253.6,"Verse 17, and the Spirit and the bride say, Come."],[2258.0,"And let him who hears say, Come, and let him who thirsts come."],[2262.56,"Whoever desires, let him take the water of life freely."],[2266.88,"This is that language from St."],[2268.08,"John's Gospel again."],[2270.46,"Anyone who comes to Christ, he'll give the living water."],[2274.62,"That's connected to baptism."],[2278.82,"Begin the life in Christ."],[2282.98,"Verse 18, for I testify to everyone who hears the words of the prophecy of this book."],[2288.02,"If anyone adds to these things, God will add to him the plagues that are written in this book."],[2292.98,"And if anyone takes away from the words of the book of this prophecy, God shall take away his part from the book of life, from the holy city, and from the things which are written in this book."],[2305.38,"le This is referring to the book of Revelation, not the Bib."],[2314.14,"When these words were written by St."],[2315.66,"John, there was not a Bible."],[2319.78,"A book between two covers. in which Revelation was the last book"],[2325.82,"In fact, that kind of Bible doesn't show up until like the 5th century."],[2330.14,"So, that has Revelation as the last book, at least."],[2334.8,"Maybe the late fourth in some places, but we're talking a long time."],[2342.0,"This is talking about this."],[2346.24,"And what's he saying?"],[2350.25,"He's basically saying, that anyone who tries to, what does it mean to take away or to add to this?"],[2357.15,"He doesn't mean literally like, hey man, if you're copying this book, don't mess up."],[2361.47,"Or curse be upon you."],[2364.59,"The idea is in terms of what is being preached."],[2369.13,"What is being proclaimed and what is what is being lived out."],[2373.9,"That this is pointing us to truth."],[2377.82,"If you want to try and massage that, get rid of parts you don't like, add parts you do like."],[2382.84,"That he's saying that's gonna be a sign that you're not overcoming, shall we say."],[2389.26,"That you're giving in to the passions of the world."],[2391.74,"You're giving in, and that's not allowing you to right embrace the fullness of Christ's revelation."],[2403.5,"Verse 20, he who testifies to these things says, surely I am coming quickly."],[2407.9,"ickly Qu. Even so, come, Lord Jesus"],[2411.54,"Amen. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all."],[2418.42,"Amen. So that's how it ends, with another reminder."],[2426.5,"Pay attention to this."],[2429.22,"Right now. This is for you right now."],[2431.62,"And then sort of a usual benediction."],[2434.42,"So that's the end of Revelation of St."],[2438.1,"John. It's the end of the Bible."],[2442.14,"Uh technically, it's twelve and a half years since I started with Genesis 1 1 in another state."],[2452.42,"But we've gone through the whole Bible, so yeah, we'll be starting over with Genesis."],[2453.38,"So thank you, everybody"],[2460.62,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2467.98,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2473.34,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.24,"lv":2,"h":"21:1 - New heaven and new earth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rev 21:1</b> read: new heaven, new earth; first <b>passed away</b>; <b>no more sea</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Sorry, beachgoers\" - not what it means</li><li class=\"d0\">Old heaven/earth \"<b>ran away</b>\" from God on the throne, scampered off</li><li class=\"d0\">Not the <b>physical earth</b> (then it'd be physical heaven) → = the <b>order of creation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why \"heaven and earth\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 1:1</b> (coming in a couple weeks): \"God created the heavens and the earth\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Gen 1 not about <b>making things appear out of thin air</b> - not denying creation from nothing</li><li class=\"d1\">Gen 1 = <b>God putting things in order</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>New order in heaven</b>: no more demonic spirits - \"<b>demons out, humans in</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>New order on earth</b>: <b>justice established</b> - judgment = putting things back in order</li></ul>"},{"t":121.76,"lv":3,"h":"Good, whole, no sea","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Old order <b>corrupted by sin</b> has passed</li><li class=\"d0\">New order like the <b>original</b>: God saw everything was <b>good</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew <i>tov</i> = also <b>beautiful, whole</b> → \"we're back to that\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sea = chaos and destruction</b> → no more chaos</li><li class=\"d1\">won't repeat; <b>last cycle is over, no more cycles</b></li></ul>"},{"t":160.37,"lv":2,"h":"21:2-4 - New Jerusalem, God dwelling with men","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rev 21:2</b> read: <b>holy city, New Jerusalem</b>, from heaven, <b>prepared as a bride</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>wedding supper of the Lamb</b> language already used</li><li class=\"d0\">City = an <b>order, ordered community of humans</b> → coming down from heaven</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:3-4</b> read: <b>tabernacle of God is with men</b>, they his people; God himself with them</li><li class=\"d1\">old order of <b>suffering, sin, hardship, death</b> over</li><li class=\"d0\">Why important? Death, mourning, crying began when <b>humanity expelled from paradise</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now restored: <b>humanity in God's presence again</b></li></ul>"},{"t":254.9,"lv":2,"h":"21:5-6 - Alpha and Omega, water of life","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:5-6</b> read: \"<b>I make all things new</b>\"; \"It is done\"; <b>Alpha and Omega</b>; fountain of <b>water of life freely</b> to the thirsty</li><li class=\"d0\">Back to where we started (<b>ch. 1</b>, Alpha and Omega) → wrapping up</li><li class=\"d0\">Water of life = Christ in <b>John's Gospel</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>last great day of the feast</b>: \"let him who is thirsty come to me and drink\"</li><li class=\"d1\">also the <b>Samaritan woman</b> - living water</li><li class=\"d1\">\"same <b>St. John</b>, for anybody doubting\"</li></ul>"},{"t":330.82,"lv":2,"h":"21:7-8 - He who overcomes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:7</b> read: overcomer inherits all things; \"I will be his God, he my <b>son</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why \"son\"? Not misogyny/non-inclusive language → <b>inheritance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">in that culture <b>sons inherited</b>, pretty much only sons</li><li class=\"d1\">addressing men <b>and women</b>: they become <b>sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"sons and daughters\" would imply <b>status distinction</b> persisting in the world to come</li><li class=\"d1\">John <b>deliberately</b>, like <b>St. Paul</b> on becoming sons of God: no status difference → <b>everyone an inheritor</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>He who overcomes</b> - seen over and over in the <b>letters</b> (chs. 2-3)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:8</b>: cowardly, unbelieving, abominable, murderers, sexually immoral, sorcerers, idolaters, <b>liars</b> → <b>lake of fire, second death</b></li><li class=\"d1\">contrast with the overcomer → \"<b>some kind of struggle, and they lost</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sin, <b>the passions</b>: liar isn't one who lied once at <b>five</b>; = one who <b>gives in</b> and <b>becomes</b> a liar, a coward</li><li class=\"d1\">sexually immoral = lets <b>lust take over</b> their life rather than <b>struggling</b></li></ul>"},{"t":492.66,"lv":2,"h":"21:9-14 - The city's gates and foundations","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:9-11</b> read: one of <b>seven bowl angels</b>: \"I will show you the <b>bride, the Lamb's wife</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ties to <b>wedding supper</b></li><li class=\"d1\">carried to <b>great high mountain</b>; city descending, <b>glory of God</b>, light like <b>jasper, clear as crystal</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:12-13</b>: great high wall, <b>12 gates</b>, <b>12 angels</b>, names of <b>12 tribes</b> (the <b>sons of Israel</b>, tribes named for the 12 sons)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>3 gates</b> each: east, north, south, west</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>gateways into the kingdom = 12 tribes of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">cf. <b>Romans 10-11</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:14</b>: wall has <b>12 foundations</b>, names of the <b>12 apostles of the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d1\">parallel: <b>twelve and twelve</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Paul</b>: apostles <b>laying a foundation</b>, <b>Christ the chief cornerstone</b>, church members building on it</li><li class=\"d1\">city <b>built by God's people, the church</b></li></ul>"},{"t":634.45,"lv":2,"h":"21:15-17 - Measuring the city","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:15</b> gold reed to measure city, gates, wall</li><li class=\"d1\">picks up <b>Ezekiel's temple vision</b> (last third of Ezekiel) - \"we'll wrap around in <b>three, four years</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Ezekiel's temple read as prophetic of <b>Christ, the eternal temple</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John wants <b>imagery, numbers, symbolism</b> - <b>not literal measurements</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:16</b>: <b>12,000 furlongs</b>, length = breadth = height</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek <b>stadia</b>; 12 × 1000 → ~<b>1,500 miles</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>a giant cube</b> - \"not the <b>Borg</b> landing on Earth\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not a \"1500-mile cube city we all live in\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1000</b> = big number; <b>12</b> = gates, foundations</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:17</b>: wall <b>144 cubits</b>, \"measure of a man, that is of an <b>angel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">cubit = elbow to fingertip; <b>how big is an angel's arm? \"Beats me\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">144 = <b>12 × 12</b> → riffing off <b>12 tribes, 12 apostles</b></li></ul>"},{"t":849.02,"lv":2,"h":"21:18-21 - Gold, stones, pearls","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:18</b> read: wall <b>jasper</b>, city <b>pure gold like clear glass</b> - \"a giant gold clear cube\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:19-20</b>: foundations with <b>12 precious stones</b>: jasper, sapphire, chalcedony, emerald, sardonyx, sardius, chrysolite, beryl, topaz, chrysoprase, jacinth, amethyst</li><li class=\"d1\">matching stone to apostle: \"have fun\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Related to <b>high priest's ephod</b>: stones with names of <b>12 tribes</b> - not the same ones, don't exactly match</li><li class=\"d0\">Parallel again: <b>24 elders</b> = <b>12 patriarchs + 12 apostles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">apostles to <b>sit on 12 thrones</b> judging 12 tribes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:21</b>: <b>12 gates = 12 pearls</b>, each gate <b>one pearl</b>; street <b>pure gold, transparent glass</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one per tribe; again <b>not literal</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1017.52,"lv":3,"h":"Aside: Paul Crouch on TBN","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Light entertainment portion</b> of our Bible study\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul Crouch</b> (TBN) at a telethon: \"end times… <b>four horsemen</b> getting ready to ride out\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"pawing at them <b>streets of gold</b>, kicking up gold dust\"</li><li class=\"d1\">coming down from heaven into <b>checking accounts</b> of those who <b>write a check now</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Some level of <b>artistry and brilliance</b>\" - not sure he uses powers <b>for good</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Greatest sermon I ever heard on TBN\"; couldn't sell it as well in church <b>fun drives</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1120.0,"lv":2,"h":"21:22 - No temple","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:22</b> read: <b>no temple</b>; <b>Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple</b></li><li class=\"d0\">After the <b>measuring rod</b>, readers think <b>Ezekiel</b> measuring the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">Jerusalem is where the temple was - now none</li><li class=\"d0\">Temple = <b>place where God dwelt</b> → eternally dwells in <b>the Lamb, in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>John's Gospel</b>: other gospels record \"<b>destroy this temple, I'll rebuild in three days</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">John adds: \"<b>speaking of the temple that is his body</b>\" - \"just in case you didn't get it\" - \"parenthetical note, hello\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Direct confirmation</b> of the fathers reading <b>Ezekiel's temple</b> symbolically → <b>the incarnation</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1215.72,"lv":3,"h":"21:23-27 - No sun or moon, open gates","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:23</b> read: no need of <b>sun or moon</b>; <b>glory of God</b> illuminates, <b>the Lamb its light</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Deut 4</b>: sun, moon, stars = associated with <b>angelic powers worshipped by nations</b> - ancient world full of sun and moon gods</li><li class=\"d1\">not that the sun (<b>93 million miles</b> away) or moon ceases to exist</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>secondary intermediary powers</b>, good or bad, between God and humanity <b>no longer in the way</b> → <b>direct to God, to the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:24</b> read: <b>nations of the saved</b> walk in its light; <b>kings of the earth</b> bring glory and honor</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>Gentiles</b> walking in light of <b>God himself</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:25</b>: gates <b>never shut by day</b>, <b>no night</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no threats → <b>no need to close gates</b>; in the old world gates closed in daytime under assault</li><li class=\"d0\">Glory and honor of the nations: <b>Isaiah</b> - nations coming to <b>Jerusalem</b> to worship Israel's God</li><li class=\"d1\">John sees it happening in <b>Christianity</b>, culminating at the end</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>21:27</b>: nothing defiling, abomination or lie; only those in <b>the Lamb's book of life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"<b>come as you are</b>\" (Nirvana reference) or \"all pagans now fine\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not pagans anymore</b> - come to worship <b>the true God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bring <b>no idolatry, no dedication to conquest and war</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bring <b>what is good, pure, holy, beautiful</b> from all nations</li></ul>"},{"t":1465.53,"lv":2,"h":"22:1-5 - River and tree of life","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rev 22:1</b> read: <b>river of water of life</b>, clear as crystal, from <b>throne of God and the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Daniel 7</b>: <b>river of fire</b> from the throne = <b>judgment</b> → now clear water giving life</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>judgment and enmity are over</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:2</b>: <b>tree of life</b> in the middle of the street, either side of the river - \"try to map that out in your head\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>12 fruits</b>, one <b>each month</b>; <b>leaves for the healing of the nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tree of life <b>from paradise</b>; city connected to <b>original paradise</b> - God's presence</li><li class=\"d1\">Eden had <b>four rivers</b>; here <b>one river</b></li><li class=\"d1\">humans <b>kept away</b> so they wouldn't live forever in the fallen state</li><li class=\"d1\">now <b>everyone eating continually</b> = blessedness <b>permanent, eternal</b> - no \"oops, somebody messed up, repeat the whole thing\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Leaves heal</b> those coming in: <b>uncleanness</b> from the nations → <b>purification</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:3-5</b>: <b>no more curse</b> - curse = <b>sent out of paradise</b> → never sent out again</li><li class=\"d1\">servants serve; <b>see his face</b>; <b>name on foreheads</b>; no night, no lamp; <b>reign forever</b></li><li class=\"d1\">state of <b>blessedness in the end</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1722.88,"lv":2,"h":"22:6-7 - Shortly, quickly","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:6</b> read: words <b>faithful and true</b>; angel sent to show things that <b>must shortly take place</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Shortly</b>\" - in <b>96 AD</b>, shortly thereafter - \"not once <b>Jack Van Impe</b> has a TV show\" (Belgian, passed away, \"I keep picking on him\")</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:7</b> read: \"<b>Behold, I am coming quickly</b>\" - <b>Christ</b> speaking</li><li class=\"d1\">not a long time later after everything unfolds <b>in sequence</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ's return <b>always imminent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">scholars: \"apostles thought he'd come in their lifetime, <b>they were wrong</b>\" - <b>no</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so did <b>2nd, 3rd, 4th generations</b>, and every generation now - <b>can happen at any time</b></li><li class=\"d1\">proves they <b>didn't think a series of things</b> had to happen first</li><li class=\"d1\">even barring his appearing, we can <b>stand before him</b> - don't know the length of our lives</li></ul>"},{"t":1858.74,"lv":2,"h":"22:8-11 - Do not worship; do not seal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:8-9</b> read: John <b>falls to worship the angel</b>: \"<b>knock it off</b>… fellow servant of your brethren the prophets… <b>worship God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"angel\" can mean <b>messenger</b>; he doesn't identify as an angel → \"may be <b>John talking to himself</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:10</b> read: \"<b>do not seal</b> the words… the time is at hand\"</li><li class=\"d1\">reference to <b>Daniel</b>: told to <b>shut up the book</b> - prophecies for the future (<b>500+ years</b> after Daniel)</li><li class=\"d1\">contrast: <b>don't shut it up</b> - \"this is for <b>right now</b>, people need to read this now\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:11</b> read: \"unjust still… filthy still… righteous still… holy still\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"weird translation\" - read by <b>Johnny Cash</b> on his last album</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"stay filthy\" → <b>\"in hand\"</b>: if you're going to change, <b>do it now</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no \"be filthy, engage in uncleanness, <b>repent real quick before the end</b>\" - doesn't work that way</li></ul>"},{"t":2032.71,"lv":2,"h":"22:12-15 - Reward, commandments, outside","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:12-13</b>: \"coming quickly, my <b>reward is with me</b>, to give to everyone <b>according to his work</b>\"; <b>Alpha and Omega</b>, first and last</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:14</b>: blessed who <b>do his commandments</b> → right to <b>tree of life</b>, enter by <b>gates</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one commandment is <b>to repent</b> → sinning doesn't mean you haven't kept them <b>unless you don't repent</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:15</b>: outside are \"<b>dogs</b>\" (\"my heathen dogs\"), sorcerers, sexually immoral, murderers, idolaters, <b>whoever loves and practices a lie</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not anyone who ever told a lie → <b>loves and practices</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Diversity of language</b> for condemnation: <b>lake of fire</b>, <b>outer darkness and madness</b>, here <b>just outside</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doors open 24 hours a day → outside <b>because they want to be</b>; nothing keeping them out</li></ul>"},{"t":2143.83,"lv":2,"h":"22:16 - Root and offspring of David","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:16</b> read: \"I, Jesus, sent my angel… <b>root and offspring of David</b>, <b>bright morning star</b>\" - \"pretty direct\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Offspring = <b>Messiah, son of David</b>; but also <b>root</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Psalm 110</b> (109 LXX): <b>most quoted OT passage in the NT</b></li><li class=\"d1\">last week before crucifixion, questions to Christ; he throws one back: \"David says, <b>the Lord said to my Lord</b>, sit at my right hand… if Messiah is David's son, <b>why does he call him Lord</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Yes: <b>Davidic king</b>, \"<b>bud from Jesse's stem</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>Christ's Messiahship = root, basis, paradigm for David's</b> - because Christ is <b>eternal</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2253.6,"lv":2,"h":"22:17-21 - Come; adding and taking away; end","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:17</b> read: \"<b>The Spirit and the bride say, Come</b>… whoever desires take <b>water of life freely</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">John's Gospel again: anyone who comes to Christ gets <b>living water</b>; connected to <b>baptism</b> - <b>beginning the life in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:18-19</b> read: add → <b>plagues added</b>; take away → part taken from <b>book of life, holy city</b></li><li class=\"d1\">refers to <b>the book of Revelation, not the Bible</b> - no Bible then, no single volume ending with Revelation</li><li class=\"d1\">that kind of Bible: <b>5th century</b> (late 4th in some places)</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"if you're copying, don't mess up\" → <b>what is preached, proclaimed, lived out</b></li><li class=\"d1\">massaging it - cutting parts you dislike, adding ones you like = sign you're <b>not overcoming</b>, <b>giving in to the passions of the world</b>, not embracing <b>the fullness of Christ's revelation</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>22:20-21</b>: \"<b>Surely I am coming quickly</b>\" / \"<b>Even so, come, Lord Jesus</b>\"; <b>grace of our Lord Jesus Christ</b> - usual benediction</li><li class=\"d1\">ends with reminder: <b>pay attention, this is for you right now</b></li><li class=\"d0\">End of Revelation, <b>end of the Bible</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>12½ years</b> since <b>Genesis 1:1</b> (in another state)</li><li class=\"d1\">gone through the whole Bible → <b>starting over with Genesis</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Starting over with <b>Genesis</b> (Gen 1 in a couple of weeks)"});
